      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Paired bicycle ergometry was used in 24 anginal patients to compare the efficiency of 10-20 mg isosorbide dinitrate, 20-30 mg corinfar and 40-80 mg propranolol. Isosorbide dinitrate showed maximum efficiency in half of the patients, corinfar in 1/4, propranolol in 1/6. Isosorbide dinitrate produced an effect with the very first dose more frequently, as compared to other drugs. Heart rate patterns at rest and under the action of corinfar and isosorbide dinitrate varied in different individuals and were related to the time of onset of an exercise-induced anginal attack."},
